[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/talk/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n4_anselm"
text = "# DRAFT
# Anselm at dusk, in his chair in the infirmary (night 4, fog). Blind, guilty and terrified. He hears men on the night stair
# and says his beads. On copied keys (keys_copied) he gives the night-4 rule sideways: bar from inside, a bar has no key.
# If Thomas has named Simon (n4_thomas_simon), Anselm says there's no harm in Simon, and stops himself.
== start
(Anselm in his chair. The fog has got into the infirmary and hangs about the brazier.)
Anselm: Fog. I can smell it. Wet stone and the river. A man could walk right past you in it.
-> topics

== again
(His milky eyes settle on a place just beside your face.)
Anselm: Back again, porter? Sit.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n4_anselm_hear] What do you hear at night, Brother Anselm? -> hear
* [if keys_copied] [if not n4_anselm_keys] Someone has copied my keys, brother. -> keys
* [if n4_thomas_simon] [if not n4_anselm_simon] What do you know of Brother Simon? -> simon

== hear [set n4_anselm_hear]
Anselm: Feet on the night stair, after Compline, when every brother's abed. More than one pair.
Anselm: They walk alike. Like men who've walked together a long while.
Anselm: I lie still, and I say my beads, and I don't call out. God forgive me, I never call out.
-> topics

== keys [set n4_anselm_keys]
(He laughs, with nothing in it.)
Anselm: Copied. There were always more keys to that gate than there were porters, boy.
Anselm: If you've a guest you want to keep, tell him to bar his door from inside. A bar has no key.
-> topics

== simon [set n4_anselm_simon]
Anselm: Simon? He brings me my broth when Thomas is busy. He talks to me about his mother in Kent.
Anselm: There's no harm in Simon. Whoever told you different, ask yourself why they...
(He stops, and turns his face to the wall.)
-> topics

== leave
Anselm: Bar it at the bell, porter.
"
